  "title": "CHAPTER 4: ECONOMY OF PUNJAB",
  "order": 4,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b3wqmr4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4.1 Overview"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Agriculture forms the backbone of Punjab's economy, driven heavily by high-yielding crop varieties introduced during the Green Revolution.",
        "Punjab Agricultural University (PAU) in Ludhiana plays a crucial role in agricultural research and technological advancement across the state.",
        "Wheat and rice dominate the state's cropping pattern, contributing a massive share to the central pool of food grains.",
        "Major industrial centers include Ludhiana for textiles and bicycles, Jalandhar for sports goods, and Mohali for IT and electronics.",
        "The state power sector utilizes a combination of thermal and hydroelectric energy sources to sustain rural tube wells and industrial demand."
      ],
      "id": "y4xwb8m"
    },
