    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Punjab Agricultural University (PAU) was established in 1962 at Ludhiana and led the state's Green Revolution initiatives.",
        "Jalandhar is world-renowned for its sports goods manufacturing, whereas Mandi Gobindgarh is famously known as the 'Steel Town' of Punjab.",
        "Punjab contributes a major proportion of wheat and paddy to India's Central Pool, earning it the title 'Granary of India'."
      ],
      "id": "d14mwss"
